IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sge-p10a-359`

-- Tests of s 359 (Part 10A, Transfer of registration: registration). Every expected value is written from the text, beside the assertion,
-- before the run; none is copied from the encoding's own output. Dates are hand-counted: 1 March 2027 plus 60 days is 30 April 2027
-- (30 days left in March, 30 days into April); 10 June 2027 plus 30 days is 10 July 2027.

§ `Section 359(1): the Registrar may register`

-- Arguments: section 360 requires refusal; the entity has complied with section 358; the Registrar thinks fit.
-- Subject to section 360, upon compliance with section 358, if the Registrar thinks fit: all three gates open, so yes.
#ASSERT `s 359(1) the Registrar may register the foreign corporate entity as a company limited by shares` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Section 360 requires refusal: "Subject to section 360", so no, whatever else is true.
#ASSERT `s 359(1) the Registrar may register the foreign corporate entity as a company limited by shares` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 359(1) the Registrar may register the foreign corporate entity as a company limited by shares` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No compliance with section 358: "upon compliance" is not met, so no.
#ASSERT `s 359(1) the Registrar may register the foreign corporate entity as a company limited by shares` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 359(1) the Registrar may register the foreign corporate entity as a company limited by shares` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Compliance, no section 360 bar, but the Registrar does not think fit: the grant's "if" gate failed; the text says nothing more.
#ASSERT `s 359(1) the Registrar may register the foreign corporate entity as a company limited by shares` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 359(2): conditions`

#ASSERT `s 359(2) the registration is subject to the condition` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 359(2) the registration is subject to the condition` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 359(3): the notice of transfer of registration`

-- The duty to issue it. "Upon registration" is a trigger, not a number of days, and no consequence is stated: the s 52 input (the period of all convenient speed, as found) sets the time.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 359(3) upon registration the Registrar must issue a notice of transfer of registration` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 359(3) issue a notice of transfer of registration` AT 1

-- late: the act is done on day 400, past the 7 days the input is, so BREACH
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 359(3) upon registration the Registrar must issue a notice of transfer of registration` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 359(3) issue a notice of transfer of registration` AT 400

-- The Registrar issues a certificate instead of the notice: not the act the duty asks for, so the duty stands.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 359(3) upon registration the Registrar must issue a notice of transfer of registration` 45 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 359(4) issue a certificate of confirmation of registration` AT 1

-- (a), (b), (c) on their own.
#ASSERT `s 359(3)(a) the notice states that the company is registered by way of transfer of registration` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 359(3)(a) the notice states that the company is registered by way of transfer of registration` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 359(3)(b) the notice states that the company is a company limited by shares` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 359(3)(b) the notice states that the company is a company limited by shares` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c) "where applicable": the company is a private company and the notice says so; or it is a private company and the notice does not.
#ASSERT `s 359(3)(c) the notice states that the company is a private company where that applies` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 359(3)(c) the notice states that the company is a private company where that applies` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Where the company is not a private company (c) does not apply, and the text says nothing about what the notice states then.
#ASSERT `s 359(3)(c) the notice states that the company is a private company where that applies` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The whole subsection. Arguments: in the prescribed form; the date specified; (a) stated; (b) stated; the company is private; (c) stated.
#ASSERT `s 359(3) the notice of transfer of registration is as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A company that is not private: (c) is not needed.
#ASSERT `s 359(3) the notice of transfer of registration is as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Each requirement missing in turn: "must issue a notice ... in the prescribed form stating ...".
#ASSERT `s 359(3) the notice of transfer of registration is as the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 359(3) the notice of transfer of registration is as the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 359(3) the notice of transfer of registration is as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 359(3) the notice of transfer of registration is as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 359(3) the notice of transfer of registration is as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 359(4): the certificate of confirmation of registration`

-- Arguments: the entity has been registered; the company has applied.
#ASSERT `s 359(4) the Registrar is required to issue a certificate of confirmation of registration` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Registered, but no application yet: "upon the application of the company", so no duty to issue yet.
#ASSERT `s 359(4) the Registrar is required to issue a certificate of confirmation of registration` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not registered: there is no "company" to apply, and the text says nothing.
#ASSERT `s 359(4) the Registrar is required to issue a certificate of confirmation of registration` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 359(4) the Registrar is required to issue a certificate of confirmation of registration` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 359(4) the Registrar must issue a certificate of confirmation of registration upon the application of the company` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 359(4) issue a certificate of confirmation of registration` AT 5

-- late: the act is done on day 400, past the 7 days the input is, so BREACH
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 359(4) the Registrar must issue a certificate of confirmation of registration upon the application of the company` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 359(4) issue a certificate of confirmation of registration` AT 400

-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 359(4) the Registrar must issue a certificate of confirmation of registration upon the application of the company` 45 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 359(3) issue a notice of transfer of registration` AT 5

§ `Section 359(5): conclusive evidence`

-- Arguments: a notice under (3); a certificate under (4).
#ASSERT `s 359(5)(a) the document is conclusive evidence that the foreign corporate entity is registered under section 359` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 359(5)(a) the document is conclusive evidence that the foreign corporate entity is registered under section 359` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Any other document: the subsection names two and is silent on the rest.
#ASSERT `s 359(5)(a) the document is conclusive evidence that the foreign corporate entity is registered under section 359` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b) the date the document states is conclusive of the date of registration.
#ASSERT `s 359(5)(b) the date of the company's registration that the document conclusively shows` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2027)
#ASSERT `s 359(5)(b) the date of the company's registration that the document conclusively shows` FALSE TRUE (Date 15 3 2027) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 3 2027)
#ASSERT `s 359(5)(b) the date of the company's registration that the document conclusively shows` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 359(6): evidence of deregistration in the place of incorporation`

-- Arguments for the last day: the notice issued on; the Registrar extended the period; the last day of the extended period.
-- 60 days after 1 March 2027 is 30 April 2027.
#ASSERT `s 359(6) the last day for submitting the document evidencing deregistration` (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE (Date 30 6 2027) EQUALS Date 30 4 2027
-- The Registrar extended the period to 30 June 2027: that is the last day.
#ASSERT `s 359(6) the last day for submitting the document evidencing deregistration` (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE (Date 30 6 2027) EQUALS Date 30 6 2027

-- Arguments for the helper: notice issued on; extended; the extended last day; the day the document is submitted.
-- Both sides of the last day (30 April 2027), and a day inside.
#ASSERT `s 359(6) the day is within the time allowed for submitting the document` (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE (Date 30 6 2027) (Date 30 4 2027)
#ASSERT NOT `s 359(6) the day is within the time allowed for submitting the document` (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE (Date 30 6 2027) (Date 1 5 2027)
#ASSERT `s 359(6) the day is within the time allowed for submitting the document` (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE (Date 30 6 2027) (Date 2 3 2027)
-- Extended to 30 June 2027: 1 May is now in time, 30 June is the last day, 1 July is late.
#ASSERT `s 359(6) the day is within the time allowed for submitting the document` (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE (Date 30 6 2027) (Date 1 5 2027)
#ASSERT `s 359(6) the day is within the time allowed for submitting the document` (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE (Date 30 6 2027) (Date 30 6 2027)
#ASSERT NOT `s 359(6) the day is within the time allowed for submitting the document` (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE (Date 30 6 2027) (Date 1 7 2027)

-- Compliance. Arguments: notice issued on; extended; extended last day; the document has been submitted; the date it was submitted; the date asked.
-- Submitted on the last day: in time.
#ASSERT `s 359(6) the foreign corporate entity has complied with the duty to submit the document evidencing deregistration` (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE (Date 30 6 2027) TRUE (Date 30 4 2027) (Date 1 8 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Submitted the day after the last day: out of time. The text fixes the period in its own words.
#ASSERT `s 359(6) the foreign corporate entity has complied with the duty to submit the document evidencing deregistration` (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE (Date 30 6 2027) TRUE (Date 1 5 2027) (Date 1 8 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not submitted: asked on the last day the period is still running (neither met nor missed); asked the day after, it has been missed.
#ASSERT `s 359(6) the foreign corporate entity has complied with the duty to submit the document evidencing deregistration` (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE (Date 30 6 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 30 4 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 359(6) the foreign corporate entity has complied with the duty to submit the document evidencing deregistration` (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE (Date 30 6 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 5 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- With the extension to 30 June 2027: submitted 1 May is in time; not submitted and asked 1 May is still running; asked 1 July it is missed.
#ASSERT `s 359(6) the foreign corporate entity has complied with the duty to submit the document evidencing deregistration` (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE (Date 30 6 2027) TRUE (Date 1 5 2027) (Date 1 8 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 359(6) the foreign corporate entity has complied with the duty to submit the document evidencing deregistration` (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE (Date 30 6 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 5 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 359(6) the foreign corporate entity has complied with the duty to submit the document evidencing deregistration` (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE (Date 30 6 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 7 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 359(6) the foreign corporate entity has complied with the duty to submit the document evidencing deregistration` (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE (Date 30 6 2027) TRUE (Date 1 7 2027) (Date 1 8 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The duty as a regulative rule: 60 days from the notice (AT 0). The submission on day 60 is in time ...
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 359(6) the foreign corporate entity registered under this section must submit the document evidencing deregistration` "Acme Pte. Ltd." 60 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte. Ltd." DOES `s 359(6) submit to the Registrar a document evidencing that the foreign corporate entity has been deregistered in its place of incorporation` AT 60

-- ... nothing done and the clock reaches day 61: the 60 days have run out, so the duty is breached.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 359(6) the foreign corporate entity registered under this section must submit the document evidencing deregistration` "Acme Pte. Ltd." 60 AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 61

-- Submitted on day 61: too late, so breached.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 359(6) the foreign corporate entity registered under this section must submit the document evidencing deregistration` "Acme Pte. Ltd." 60 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte. Ltd." DOES `s 359(6) submit to the Registrar a document evidencing that the foreign corporate entity has been deregistered in its place of incorporation` AT 61

-- The Registrar extended the period to 90 days: day 75 is in time, day 91 is not.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 359(6) the foreign corporate entity registered under this section must submit the document evidencing deregistration` "Acme Pte. Ltd." 90 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte. Ltd." DOES `s 359(6) submit to the Registrar a document evidencing that the foreign corporate entity has been deregistered in its place of incorporation` AT 75

-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 359(6) the foreign corporate entity registered under this section must submit the document evidencing deregistration` "Acme Pte. Ltd." 90 AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 91

§ `Section 359(7): the Registrar may extend the 60 days`

-- Arguments: the entity is registered; it has applied for the extension.
#ASSERT `s 359(7) the Registrar may extend the 60-day period` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No application: "on the application of", so no power under this subsection.
#ASSERT `s 359(7) the Registrar may extend the 60-day period` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not a registered entity: the text says nothing.
#ASSERT `s 359(7) the Registrar may extend the 60-day period` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 359(8): waive or modify a condition`

#ASSERT `s 359(8) the Registrar may waive or modify the condition` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 359(8) the Registrar may waive or modify the condition` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 359(9): appeal to the Minister`

-- Arguments: aggrieved; the decision; the date of the decision; the date of the appeal. The decision is dated 10 June 2027, so 30 days
-- after it ends on 10 July 2027.
#ASSERT `s 359(9) the person aggrieved may appeal to the Minister` TRUE `s 359(9)(a) the refusal of the Registrar to register a foreign corporate entity under subsection (1)` (Date 10 6 2027) (Date 20 6 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 359(9) the person aggrieved may appeal to the Minister` TRUE `s 359(9)(a) the refusal of the Registrar to register a foreign corporate entity under subsection (1)` (Date 10 6 2027) (Date 10 7 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 359(9) the person aggrieved may appeal to the Minister` TRUE `s 359(9)(a) the refusal of the Registrar to register a foreign corporate entity under subsection (1)` (Date 10 6 2027) (Date 11 7 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The same 30 days run from the imposition of a condition (b) and from the modification of a condition (c).
#ASSERT `s 359(9) the person aggrieved may appeal to the Minister` TRUE `s 359(9)(b) a condition of registration imposed by the Registrar under subsection (2)` (Date 10 6 2027) (Date 10 7 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 359(9) the person aggrieved may appeal to the Minister` TRUE `s 359(9)(b) a condition of registration imposed by the Registrar under subsection (2)` (Date 10 6 2027) (Date 11 7 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 359(9) the person aggrieved may appeal to the Minister` TRUE `s 359(9)(c) the modification of a condition by the Registrar under subsection (8)` (Date 10 6 2027) (Date 10 7 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 359(9) the person aggrieved may appeal to the Minister` TRUE `s 359(9)(c) the modification of a condition by the Registrar under subsection (8)` (Date 10 6 2027) (Date 11 7 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A decision that is none of the three: the right is given against those three only by its own words, and the text says nothing of others.
#ASSERT `s 359(9) the person aggrieved may appeal to the Minister` TRUE `s 359(9) some other decision` (Date 10 6 2027) (Date 20 6 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A person not aggrieved: the right is "Any person aggrieved", and the text says nothing of anyone else.
#ASSERT `s 359(9) the person aggrieved may appeal to the Minister` FALSE `s 359(9)(a) the refusal of the Registrar to register a foreign corporate entity under subsection (1)` (Date 10 6 2027) (Date 20 6 2027) EQUALS NOTHING

-- "whose decision is final".
#ASSERT `s 359(9) the Minister's decision on the appeal is final` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 359(9) the Minister's decision on the appeal is final` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The appeal as a permission within 30 days: taken up on day 30, it is fulfilled. Unused, it lapses without consequence (a permission has no breach).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 359(9) a person aggrieved may appeal to the Minister within 30 days` "Lim Wei" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "Lim Wei" DOES `s 359(9) appeal to the Minister` AT 30

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 359(9) a person aggrieved may appeal to the Minister within 30 days` "Lim Wei" AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 31
